  "description": "ANSI escape codes break style()\n\nWhen using `style()` or `secho()` to write colored logs on the shell, it can sometimes be short-circuited if the log we try to apply color to is already colored with ANSI escape codes. \n\nThis is an issue when trying to color output from a file for example, when you want to highlight certain words (think of grep).\n\n## Replicate\n```\nansi_red = \"\\033[0;31m\"\nansi_endcolor = \"\\033[0m\"\nclick.secho(f\"{ansi_red}This should be blue{ansi_endcolor}\", fg=\"blue\")\n```\n### output :\n$\\color{red}\\textsf{This should be blue}$\n\n### Expected output :\n$\\color{blue}\\textsf{This should be blue}$\n\nEnvironment:\n\n- Python version: 3.9.25\n- Click version: 8.1.8\n\n_Also present in latest :_\n\n- Python version: 3.10.0\n- Click version: 8.5.0",
